            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, the case Kircher v. Putnam Funds Trust concerns whether the general rule prohibiting appealability applies."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners and Respondents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-90c1760a468a-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-90c1760a468a-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The parties dispute the scope of the Securities Litigation Uniform Standards Act (SLUSA) and whether it precludes certain state\u2011law claims."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-90c1760a468a-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The petitioners argue that the general rule prohibiting appealability applies in this case for three reasons."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. PERRY",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-90c1760a468a-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 27,
                "start": 27
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. PERRY, the petitioners contend that SLUSA precludes precisely what subsection (b) says it precludes, which is beyond the scope of 10b\u20115."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-90c1760a468a-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 39,
                "start": 39
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The petitioners argue that if a State court gave preclusive effect to the Federal court judgment, the collateral estoppel question would be open to review."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. FREDERICK",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-90c1760a468a-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 22,
                "start": 22
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. FREDERICK, mr. Frederick states that Congress has decided there is a paramount interest in having decisions made on their merits, which is why there is no appellate review of remand orders."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-90c1760a468a-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 57,
                "start": 57
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Frederick, mr. Frederick asserts that a complaint alleging negligent use of manipulative devices would be covered by SLUSA and thus preempted."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-90c1760a468a-0003-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 58,
                "start": 58
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Mr. Frederick further argues that the district court was wrong in not anticipating Dabit, but not wrong regarding subject\u2011matter jurisdiction because the case is based on negligence, not fraud."
        }
      ],
